on carcharias"], "bullkelp>rockfish": ["g", "Sebastes", "Nereocystis luetkeana"], "kelpcrab>rockfish": ["g", "Sebastes", "Pugettia producta"], "giantkelp>orca": ["g", "Orcinus orca", "Macrocystis pyrifera"], "rockfish>orca": ["g", "Orcinus orca", "Sebastes"]}, "story": "In ideal conditions, giant kelp grows 30–60 cm a day and forms a forest that shelters many animals. Urchins, abalone and kelp crabs eat the kelp. Sea otters eat all three, and sunflower sea stars eat urchins and abalone.", "matters": "Kelp is called an ecosystem engineer because it provides the physical home for the whole community. It grows fastest in upwelling months and dies back when nutrients drop, days shorten or storms increase."}